;; Settings for running the server against a shadow-cljs watch, read on
;; top of the built-in resources/config.edn:
;;   CORPUS_PROBE_CONFIG=dev/watch.edn clojure -M -m dk.cst.corpus-probe.server
;;
;; Deliberately not named config.edn. The :dev alias puts dev/ on the
;; classpath, where a second config.edn shadows the built-in one that
;; read-config looks up by name, and the server then starts with no
;; registry at all.
;;
;; Nothing here reaches a packaged jar: dev/ is not a source path.
{;; the origin a shadow-cljs watch pushes recompiled code from. It widens
 ;; the Content-Security-Policy to let that socket through and to allow
 ;; the eval its module loader does; absent, the policy stays strict.
 :dev-client "ws://localhost:9630"}
